WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.440
There weren’t very many people . . . many schools playing night football at that time.

2
00:00:04.440 --> 00:00:08.640
So when we broadcast games at night, we had a nationwide audience.

3
00:00:08.640 --> 00:00:11.020
LSU enjoyed the fruits of that.

4
00:00:11.020 --> 00:00:18.380
I think the radio broadcasts of the LSU games throughout the 1960s and ’70s particularly were very,

5
00:00:18.380 --> 00:00:24.600
very important, extremely important in building the image of LSU in the athletic sense.

6
00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:28.520
And also letting people throughout the country know that it’s . . . you know,

7
00:00:28.520 --> 00:00:33.900
that people do live down here and it is a great place.

8
00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:38.760
And that’s one of the . . . Those are things we tried to impart through our broadcast.

9
00:00:38.760 --> 00:00:40.824
We just didn’t go describe the plays.

10
00:00:40.824 --> 00:00:45.980
We were selling . . . we were selling the state, we were selling the region,

11
00:00:45.980 --> 00:00:50.567
we were selling LSU, we were selling . . . We really were sales people.
